cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its evidence, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Financial ABM: an auditable multi-agent artificial market for ESG disclosure and greenwashing policy experiments"
abstract: >-
  An agent-based artificial financial market in which profit-maximizing and impact investors
  evolve by imitation, firms choose between real improvement, greenwashing and maintenance,
  and a regulator sets transparency, audits and fines. The disclosure domain (ESG, AI-washing, ...)
  is a configuration file. Version 0.2.0 adds the pre-registered stage F experiment (59 scenarios x 30
  paired seeds): information policy ranks above penalty policy and baseline at both ends of the
  natural-decay range, with magnitudes reported as that range; and a static browser sandbox whose firm
  decision rule is cross-checked against the Python model. Results are conditional on the model.
